---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Snippet from "../components/Snippet.astro";
import { BLOB, href } from "../site";

const CORE = `
import { computed, effect, get, signal, update } from "reflex-quant";

const tick = signal(0);
const pulse = grid.map(() => signal(0));              // one inbox per firefly

const firefly = grid.map((_, i) => computed((prev) => {
  const t = get(tick);
  let phase = prev.phase + (t - prev.tick) * 0.01;    // time advances once per tick
  let lit = prev.lit;

  const incoming = get(pulse[i]);
  if (incoming) {
    update(pulse[i], () => 0);                         // consume the inbox
    if (t - lit > 30) phase += incoming;               // refractory after a flash
  }
  if (phase >= 1) {                                    // flash: reset, kick the neighbours
    phase = 0;
    lit = t;
    for (const j of near[i]) update(pulse[j], (x) => x + 0.11);   // whoever sees it now
  }
  return { tick: t, phase, lit };
}, { tick: 0, phase: Math.random(), lit: -Infinity }));

effect(() => { for (const f of firefly) get(f); });   // the solver

const step = () => update(tick, (t) => t + 1);`;

const STATEFUL = `
// Without prev: the oscillator's state needs its own signals
const phase = grid.map(() => signal(Math.random()));
const lit = grid.map(() => signal(-Infinity));
// ...and the computation reads them and writes them back: a feedback loop in the graph`;
---
<Base
  path="/fireflies/"
  title="Firefly Synchronization with JavaScript Signals | Reflex Quant"
  headline="Fireflies: a fixpoint without a loop"
  description="600 flying fireflies synchronized by Reflex Quant. Each firefly's phase lives in its computed's previous value, flashes are writes, and the avalanche is solved by the reactive runtime with no event queue."
  kind="Article"
  theme="night"
>
  <svg width="0" height="0" style="position:absolute" aria-hidden="true">
    <defs>
      <marker id="dg-a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0L10,5L0,10z" class="dg-ah" /></marker>
      <marker id="dg-w" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0L10,5L0,10z" class="dg-wh" /></marker>
    </defs>
  </svg>

  <p class="lede">Each firefly is a <code>computed</code> whose phase lives in <code>prev</code>. A flash writes to its neighbours' inboxes from inside that computation. There is no event queue and no stabilization loop: the runtime's invalidations are the loop.</p>

  <figure class="life" data-fireflies>
    <canvas aria-label="Field of fireflies. Click one to make it flash."></canvas>
    <div class="life-bar">
      <button type="button" data-act="play">▶ Play</button>
      <button type="button" data-act="step">Step</button>
      <button type="button" data-act="scramble">Scramble</button>
      <span class="life-tip">click a firefly to poke it</span>
    </div>
    <dl class="life-stats ff-stats" aria-live="off">
      <div><dt>tick</dt><dd data-tick>0</dd></div>
      <div><dt>flashed</dt><dd data-lit>–</dd></div>
      <div><dt>computed runs</dt><dd data-runs>–</dd></div>
      <div><dt>pulses sent</dt><dd data-pulses>–</dd></div>
      <div><dt>driver runs</dt><dd data-passes>–</dd></div>
      <div><dt>ms</dt><dd data-ms>–</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <div class="ff-front-h">fireflies executed per driver run, last step (each bar runs until the next driver run starts, validation included)</div>
    <div class="ff-front" data-frontier></div>
  </figure>
  <p>They start at random phases and flash on their own. A firefly that sees a flash is nudged forward; one pushed over the edge flashes with the one that pushed it and stays in step. Swarms fall into step first, then the whole field: within a few hundred ticks all 600 flash together. On the way there, one <code>step()</code> can carry an avalanche across hundreds of fireflies. Press <strong>Step</strong> during a wave and read the bars under the counters.</p>

  <h2>How they fly</h2>
  <p>The flight follows what is known about <em>Photinus</em> fireflies, simplified:</p>
  <ul class="fingers">
    <li><strong>Males fly</strong> slowly and low over the grass on wandering paths, and stay near where they emerged, so they gather in swarms.</li>
    <li><strong>A flash comes with a swoop up</strong>, the "J" stroke of <em>P. pyralis</em>: the light traces a short climb.</li>
    <li><strong>Females mostly perch</strong> in the grass and flash from there. About one in five here does not fly.</li>
    <li><strong>Synchronous species</strong> such as <em>P. carolinus</em> flash in short bursts and then go dark together. Each burst here is three quick flashes.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The flight is ordinary code, not reactive state. It decides one thing: who is close enough to see whose flash, up to the 8 nearest within reach. When a firefly flashes it writes to whoever is near <em>at that moment</em>. Those are writes, not reads, so the reactive graph stays the same while everything flies: three edges per firefly, whoever its neighbours are.</p>

  <h2>The whole simulation</h2>
  <Snippet code={CORE} />
  <p>That is all of it. The demo adds one more signal, <code>epoch</code>, so <strong>Scramble</strong> can restart every firefly.</p>

  <h2>The model is cyclic. The dependency graph is not.</h2>
  <figure class="dg">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 680 270" role="img" aria-label="Left: fireflies A, B and C excite each other in a loop. Right: Quant's graph has tick and one inbox feeding each firefly, and every firefly feeding the solver; the flashes are dashed writes into inboxes, not edges.">
      <text x="20" y="22" class="dg-h">what happens</text>
      <circle cx="90" cy="95" r="24" class="dg-n hot" /><text x="90" y="100" text-anchor="middle">A</text>
      <circle cx="230" cy="95" r="24" class="dg-n hot" /><text x="230" y="100" text-anchor="middle">B</text>
      <circle cx="160" cy="205" r="24" class="dg-n hot" /><text x="160" y="210" text-anchor="middle">C</text>
      <path d="M116,88 Q160,62 204,88" class="dg-wl" marker-end="url(#dg-w)" /><text x="160" y="62" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-s">flash</text>
      <path d="M232,122 Q222,175 186,197" class="dg-wl" marker-end="url(#dg-w)" /><text x="238" y="172" class="dg-s">flash</text>
      <path d="M134,200 Q92,178 86,122" class="dg-wl" marker-end="url(#dg-w)" /><text x="40" y="172" class="dg-s">flash</text>
      <text x="20" y="258" class="dg-s">a real feedback loop: A → B → C → A</text>

      <line x1="320" y1="14" x2="320" y2="262" class="dg-sep" />

      <text x="345" y="22" class="dg-h">what Quant stores</text>
      <rect x="465" y="34" width="90" height="24" class="dg-b" /><text x="510" y="51" text-anchor="middle">tick</text>
      <rect x="370" y="88" width="80" height="24" class="dg-b" /><text x="410" y="105" text-anchor="middle">inbox A</text>
      <rect x="470" y="88" width="80" height="24" class="dg-b" /><text x="510" y="105" text-anchor="middle">inbox B</text>
      <rect x="570" y="88" width="80" height="24" class="dg-b" /><text x="610" y="105" text-anchor="middle">inbox C</text>
